        <h4 class="cag-h4">Does the Price Include DNA Sexing and Health Screening?</h4>
        <p>Both, on every bird, with no separate line. Our <a href="/dna-tested-african-grey-for-sale/">DNA-tested Greys page</a> explains how the PCR sexing works and what the certificate proves, and the same sample run covers the PBFD and Polyomavirus screening we do before any bird is offered.</p>

        <h5 class="cag-h5">Paperwork We Price Into the Bird, Never Bill Afterwards</h5>
        <p>Five documents travel with every Grey we place. A seller who charges for these separately is not offering you a cheaper bird — they are offering you the same bird with the invoice split in two, and the second half arrives after you have committed.</p>

        <h6 class="cag-h6">Line Item: Hatch Certificate, CITES File, PCR Results, Vet Certificate</h6>
        <p>The hatch certificate carries the closed leg-band number; the CITES Appendix I captive-bred file establishes lawful origin; the DNA certificate names the sex; the PCR panel covers PBFD and Polyomavirus; and the avian-vet health certificate is dated within ten days of travel. <a href="/african-greys-for-sale-with-health-guarantee/">The guarantee attached to every price</a> sets out what happens if any of it fails to match the bird.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">What Does the Deposit Hold, and When Is the Balance Due?</h3>
        <p>A deposit takes a named bird off the board and starts the paperwork; the balance falls due before we book travel. We keep that gap deliberately, because it is the window in which sensible buyers order the cage — and because a bird held without a deposit is a bird two families are quietly counting on.</p>

