        <h5 class="cag-h5">Buying the Cage Twice Is the Most Common First-Year Mistake</h5>
        <p>We watch it happen most years. Somebody buys a mid-size cage for a baby Grey, the bird grows into a full-sized Congo with a full-sized wingspan, and eight months later there is a second cage in the hallway and a first one on a resale site at half price.</p>

        <h3 class="cag-h3">What Recurs Every Year for the Next Forty?</h3>
        <p>Food, veterinary care, replacement enrichment and a contingency — {range(annualRun)} a year, every year. Our <a href="/best-african-grey-parrot-food/">guide to the pellet brands we actually feed</a> covers the diet side, which is the largest predictable slice of that figure.</p>

